```cpp
std::string markdownToHtml(std::string markdown) {
    // Convert markdown to html
    std::string html = "<!DOCTYPE html><html><head></head><body>";
    html += "<h1>Markdown to HTML Converter</h1>";
    html += "<p>This program converts Markdown to HTML.</p>";
    html += "<p>Enter a markdown string:</p>";
    std::string input = std::cin.getline(std::cin.tie(), '\n', '\r');
    html += "<p>Input:</p>";
    html += input;
    html += "</body></html>";
    return html;
}
```

This function takes a reference to a std::string containing markdown formatted text and returns a std::string containing html formatted text. It first converts the input string to an HTML string using the `std::string` constructor. It then loops through each line of the input string and converts each line to an HTML paragraph using the `std::string` constructor. Finally, it concatenates the HTML paragraphs into a single HTML string.

To use this function, simply call it with a reference to a std::string containing markdown formatted text:

```cpp
std::string input = "## Hello, world!";
std::string html = markdownToHtml(input);
std::cout << html << std::endl;
```

